  - path: docs/use-cases/web-ui.html
    tier: T2
    action: updated
    distills: >-
      UC-4 gains a new block, "The capture-management controls" (id uc-4-capture-controls), stating what a
      user of the native app can now do that they could not: the app's FIRST controls that change server
      state, behind one ⋮ trigger at the header's trailing edge past the filters that scope them, beside a
      fixed-width slot reading the count those filters selected and reading "exporting…"/"importing…" while
      a transfer runs - the same box either way, so starting one moves nothing else in the row. A three-row
      table, one per act: export as har… gives the filtered capture through the OS save dialog under the
      filename THE SERVER stamped rather than one the app invented, and dismissing that dialog is an
      outcome not a failure (the line clears and nothing claims a file was written); import… is one modal
      taking either way in - a chosen .har file, or a curl command pasted into the target it opens focused
      on - whose refusal is the server's own sentence shown verbatim under the text that caused it with
      that text left in place to edit (links DEC-37); clear… is a modal ask titled with the count it will
      remove whose initial focus is on the answer that does nothing, with the consequence carrying the only
      alarm on the screen and the button carrying none. Then the two things the list itself gained: an
      imported row carries a ↑ mark in its time cell with its own accessible name, so a capture someone
      handed you is tellable from live traffic WITHOUT a column of its own (links DEC-36); and a cleared
      list gets a third absence of its own, "capture cleared", with the same remedy the never-captured one
      gives, because after a clear the remedy genuinely is the same and the heading is what says which
      nothing this is. Closes with the rule that binds all three: they refill the list from the event bus,
      never from their own response, because the responses carry counts rather than rows and two sources of
      truth for one list is a race - which is what the `cleared` event exists for. UC-6's and UC-7's
      provenance callouts each now name the route a person takes to what they already offered a client,
      replacing the placeholder both carried ("the app's own controls follow in the same epic") with a link
      to UC-4's block and the W6 badge. Header to v10 and the E-EXPORT attribution widened to name UC-4's
      capture-management controls.
