  each gaining one cross-link where they previously deferred to a WU that had not happened yet. No new
  decision record and no rulebook change: every reason this WU could have written down was already
  decided and recorded by design run 11, and copying it down a tier is the duplication the tier system
  forbids - the result cites the run instead. T1 architecture.html was re-read at close and NOT edited:
  its UI seam says the native app is an out-of-process client of the control API, and a client that also
  POSTs and DELETEs is still exactly that; no store, module or event contract moved in this WU. One fact
